Conflicts: wpasupplicant
Replaces: wpasupplicant
Provides: wpasupplicant
Description: Client for Wi-Fi Protected Access (WPA) - Qualcomm build
 WPA supplicant client built from Qualcomm source (external/wpa_supplicant_8,
 v2.12-devel) with QCA-specific features enabled via defconfig-qcacld.
 .
 Enabled QCA features (vs Ubuntu wpasupplicant 2.10):
  - CONFIG_DRIVER_NL80211_QCA: QCA vendor nl80211 extensions
  - CONFIG_WAPI / CONFIG_WAPI_AP: WAPI authentication support
  - CONFIG_IEEE80211BE: Wi-Fi 7 (EHT/802.11be) preliminary support
  - CONFIG_SAE_PK / CONFIG_OCV: WPA3 R3 features
  - CONFIG_MARKER: Boot KPI marker support
  - CONFIG_NO_ROAMING: Disable roaming (automotive use case)
  - CONFIG_MBO / CONFIG_WNM / CONFIG_ACS: Additional AP features
 .
 Replaces the Ubuntu wpasupplicant package.
